import{NEWS_KEY as h,esc as e,lsSet as d,markNews as l,openSheet as c}from"core";const t=[{id:"2026-11-13c",date:"Nov 13",items:[["Alerts for your players and your bets","Phone alerts now cover more than your team. Players you starred: a 30, 40 or 50-point game, a triple-double, and their final line. Tracked bets: each leg as it hits or misses (with how many are left on a parlay), a leg that's one away late in a game, an under that's in danger, and when the whole thing cashes. Both come with Fullcourt closed, and both have their own switch in Settings under Game alerts. Bet alerts cover legs tied to a game on the schedule."],["Smoother phone menu","The menu on phones no longer runs off the bottom on smaller screens: the list scrolls with a soft fade, items are spaced evenly, the league switch fills the width, and the slide-in animation is quicker and doesn't stutter (the blur behind it was the heavy part on phones and is gone)."]]},{id:"2026-11-13b",date:"Nov 13",items:[["Stays light when left open","Every game or player you opened, and every visit to the Bet Desk, used to stay in memory after you closed it, for as long as Fullcourt was open. After a day in the Windows app that added up to tens of thousands of hidden page pieces. Closed panels are now let go of, so memory stays level however long it runs. Leaving the Bet Desk before it finished loading also used to leave its loading paused in the background, to wake up again with the next visit and fetch everything twice; it now stops."]]},{id:"2026-11-13a",date:"Nov 13",items:[["Game alerts with Fullcourt closed","Turn on the bell next to your team and alerts now reach your phone or computer even when Fullcourt isn't open: tip-off, overtime, a close finish (within 5 in the last 5 minutes) and the final with the top scorers. On iPhone and iPad this works from the Home Screen app (iOS 16.4 or later). Settings has a new Game alerts section with a test button and an option for a heads-up on any close finish in the league, whoever is playing. The Windows app keeps sending alerts while it runs in the tray."]]},{id:"2026-11-12e",date:"Nov 12",items:[["Top scorers shows every top scorer","Points, rebounds and assists on the strip under the games came from the scoreboard, which only names each team's leader, so a teammate with 30 never showed. Once games tip off, all six stats now rank every player from the box scores (the top 20), refreshed about every 25 seconds while games are on. Before tip-off it still shows season averages. College is unchanged."]]},{id:"2026-11-12d",date:"Nov 12",items:[["Lighter and faster","The score ticker across the top of the computer layout now glides on the graphics card instead of being moved by the page's code every frame, which was most of what an open Fullcourt window used while you weren't touching it. It takes about an eighth of the processor time now, in the browser and in the Windows app. Player photos are now downloaded at the size they're shown: about a quarter of the data on a computer, and much less for small faces like the Bet Desk and Leaders lists on a phone. On a phone, the injury report under the scores (over 1 MB) now loads only when you scroll to it."]]},{id:"2026-11-12c",date:"Nov 12",items:[["Pick the stat on Top scorers","The strip of players under the games used to rank points only. It now has a row of buttons: PTS, REB, AST, STL, BLK and 3PM. Points, rebounds and assists show each team's leader and move with the live scores. Steals, blocks and threes read the box scores, so they rank every player in the day's games and refresh about every 45 seconds while games are on. Your pick is remembered. Before the first tip-off the strip shows season averages, and steals, blocks and threes wait until a game has started. College has points, rebounds and assists."]]},{id:"2026-11-12b",date:"Nov 12",items:[["Export puts your picks in the book's slip",`In the Bet Desk slip, Export used to copy your picks and open the sportsbook for you to rebuild them. For FanDuel, DraftKings, Caesars and BetMGM it now shows how many of your picks that book has at your line ("all 3 picks", "2 of 3 picks") and opens a Send sheet. On a phone, Open takes you into the book's app with those picks already in the bet slip. On a computer the sheet shows a QR code to scan with your phone, plus Copy link and a button for the book's site. Each pick also has its own link in case the book drops one. Caesars and BetMGM run a separate site per state, so the sheet asks for yours once. When a book's link for a pick doesn't say over or under (some DraftKings ones don't), that pick is left out of the count and the book opens on the right game instead. Player props only, for now; other books and pick'em apps still copy and open.`]]},{id:"2026-11-12a",date:"Nov 12",items:[["WNBA history in Ask",`In WNBA mode Ask now knows every season back to 1997, not only champions and MVPs: award races and voting by year ("2019 MVP race"), leaders ("top scorers 2008"), any two players or seasons side by side ("A'ja Wilson 2024 vs Breanna Stewart 2018"), team seasons, every draft, career totals, All-WNBA and All-Defensive teams, playoff series, franchise records, and searches across all of it ("players who averaged 20 and 10", "best rookie seasons", "highest PER ever"). Not in yet: All-Star rosters, and questions that depend on a player's age.`],["Share any answer as a picture","The share button used to appear only on the side-by-side player cards. Now any Ask answer with a list, a table or a fact sheet has one: a draft board, a list of champions, a roster, a franchise's history, career leaders, a player's bio. On a computer it copies the image; on a phone it opens the share sheet."],["Data jobs that fix themselves","On November 11 GitHub stopped handing out one kind of machine for a few hours, and the odds and highlights refreshes sat in a queue until they were cancelled. A watchdog now checks every 15 minutes and restarts any job that never got a machine on a kind that is working. The health check also flags a job that has waited more than 12 minutes."]]},{id:"2026-11-11a",date:"Nov 11",items:[["Ask understands far more",`Ask used to answer a stat line or tell you it couldn't match the question. It now reads many more kinds of question, forgives typos ("gianis", "celtcs", "wembenyama"), knows more nicknames, and keeps the thread: after "who won the 1998 Finals" you can ask "what about 1999?", and after "how tall was Shaq" you can ask "how many rings does he have?"`],["Who players are",'Height, weight, age, birthday, hometown, college, number, position, draft pick, injury status and, in the NBA, contracts: "how tall is Wemby", "Brunson contract", "is Embiid playing tonight", "highest paid player". Across the league: "who is the oldest player in the NBA", "who wears number 23", "players from Kentucky", "best rookies".'],["Teams, beyond the record",`Rosters, last game's starters, coaches, injury reports, payroll, the next meeting between two teams, the last ten games, and where a team ranks in anything: "Knicks injuries", "who coaches the Lakers", "when do the Knicks play the Celtics", "best defense", "fastest pace", "longest win streak", "best record at home". Playoff and title chances come from the season sim ("will the Knicks make the playoffs", "title odds"), and the draft from the Mock Draft ("who has the first pick", "top prospects").`],["All of NBA history",'New data behind Ask: every draft, career totals, accolades and rings, every playoff series, team ratings back to 1947, and heights, colleges and birthdays for every player who has appeared. So: "who was drafted before Jordan", "how many rings does LeBron have", "who won the 1998 Finals", "how far did the Knicks go in 1999", "what teams did Shaq play for", "how tall was Manute Bol", "Knicks history", "best record ever", "how many 60-win seasons do the Spurs have".'],["Search every season at once",'Ask can now look across all of history for seasons that fit: "players who averaged 30 and 10", "50-40-90 seasons", "rookies who averaged 20 points", "best seasons at age 19", "best seasons after 35", "youngest MVP", "last player to average 15 rebounds", "highest PER ever", "best rebounding seasons by a guard". The top results come as a card you can share.'],["Terms, rules and the calendar",'"What is true shooting", "what does PER mean", "how many fouls to foul out", "how far is the three-point line", "when is the All-Star Game". In WNBA mode Ask now knows champions, MVPs and career leaders; college mode gets rosters, coaches, team rankings and streaks.']]},{id:"2026-11-10b",date:"Nov 10",items:[["Ask knows every NBA season",`Ask used to stop at this season. It now has every player's numbers for every season back to 1947, with award voting and team records. Try "1962 MVP race", "who won Defensive Player of the Year in 2004", "top scorers 1987", "best scoring seasons ever", "1996 Bulls", or just a name like "Wilt Chamberlain".`],["Side-by-side graphics you can share",'Those answers come as a card: each player in a column with his season, photo and numbers, and a bottom row for things like MVP finish. Compare anyone across eras ("Wilt 1962 vs Jordan 1988", "LeBron, Luka and Wemby rookie seasons", "Magic vs Bird career"), up to five at a time. Every card has a Share as image button.'],["This season too",`Player comparisons ("Luka vs Ant") now use the same card, and "MVP race" or "Rookie of the Year race" shows the top of Fullcourt's ladder that way. Add "graphic" to a question about one player to get his card.`]]},{id:"2026-11-10a",date:"Nov 10",items:[["Faster all around","A tune-up release. Scores now refresh by changing only the cards whose score, clock or line moved instead of redrawing the whole page (a busy college day used to rebuild 150 cards every 15 seconds). Opening games, players and teams takes about a third of the work it did, the score ticker no longer makes the page re-measure itself 60 times a second, and bars and tables animate without stutter. Pages start loading the moment your pointer or finger lands on their button."],["Lighter on data","The Bet Desk only downloads player game logs while you're looking at it. Head to head and Ask's team questions keep finished seasons on your device, so only the current season is fetched again. College standings refresh when a game ends instead of every five minutes. On a weak signal, Fullcourt opens from its saved copy after 2.5 seconds instead of waiting on the network."],["Steadier live games","A live game page leaves itself alone when nothing has changed (timeouts, halftime), and when it does update, the box score stays scrolled where you had it."],["Sort the box score and standings","Tap any column heading in a box score (PTS, REB, +/- and the rest) to sort the players by it, and tap it again to go back. Standings sort the same way: tap PPG, OPP, L10, Strk or any column. A second tap flips the order and a third returns to the standings."],["Small things","A Today button appears next to the day's title whenever you're looking at another date. Search lists the players and teams you opened most recently before you type. In Ask, the up arrow brings back your earlier questions."],["Fixes",`Bet Desk props on phones: player names were squeezed to a letter after the projection columns arrived. Phones now show Chance and L10, with the projection under the line. Also fixed: the mock draft's Big Board running past its card, buttons sitting beside the text on "NBA only" pages, and browsers' automatic dark mode washing out player photos.`]]},{id:"2026-11-09g",date:"Nov 9",items:[["Share the day's slate","A new share button on Scores (next to the date) makes an image of the day's games: each matchup with its tip-off time (or the score and status once it starts), the spread and total, and Fullcourt's pick with its win chance, marked \u2713 or \u2717 once games end. College shows the ranked games first. It works for any day you're looking at."]]},{id:"2026-11-09f",date:"Nov 9",items:[["Fullcourt prop projections","The Bet Desk now shows Fullcourt's own number for every prop (Proj), the chance the over or under hits (Chance), and how that compares with the sportsbook's price (Value: positive means the price is better than it should be). The projection is his per-minute rate, weighted toward recent games, times his expected minutes, adjusted for the defense against his position, pace, home court, rest and blowout risk. Tap a row to see the projection and its chance at any mark."],["Ask by voice","Tap the mic beside the typing bar and ask out loud. Your words show as you talk and the question sends when you stop. In the Windows app, press Windows key + H to dictate into the box instead."]]},{id:"2026-11-09e",date:"Nov 9",items:[["Rotation on game pages","A new Rotation tab on every game shows who was on the floor and when for both teams, quarter by quarter (halves in men's college), built from the play-by-play's substitutions. Starters are marked, minutes are on the right, and it works during live games too."],["Assist map","A new Assists tab draws who assisted whom for each team: arrows from passer to scorer, thicker for more assists, plus the top passing combos and the points they made."],["More women's college highlights","Replay now also pulls women's college videos from the Big Ten women's channel, FOX's women's channel, ESPN, the American and Sun Belt conferences, and official school channels (LSU, Florida, Mississippi State, Ole Miss, Oklahoma, Alabama, Kentucky, UConn), so far more Top 25 games have a video. Longer highlight cuts show as Extended."]]},{id:"2026-11-09d",date:"Nov 9",items:[["Depth charts on team pages","Every team page now has a Depth chart above the roster, in all four leagues. NBA teams show ESPN's depth chart, point guard to center. ESPN has none for the WNBA or college, so Fullcourt builds one: the starting five from who started the last few games, then everyone else by recent minutes, as guards, forwards and centers. Starters are highlighted, minutes per game and injuries are shown, and players who are out drop to the end of their row. Tap anyone to open their page."]]},{id:"2026-11-09c",date:"Nov 9",items:[["Team questions in Ask",'Ask about any team split this season or any past one: "Knicks in back-to-backs", "Celtics at home vs the West", "Spurs after a loss", "Knicks in close games", "Thunder last season in the playoffs" or "Knicks vs Celtics history". You get the record, points for and against, and every game.'],["With and without",`"Knicks without Brunson", "Sixers when LeBron sits" and "Maxey without Embiid" show the team's record or the player's numbers with and without a teammate, plus the games he missed. Game searches show the team's record too ("Knicks when Brunson scores 30+").`],["Head to head on game pages","Every game page now shows the two teams' meetings over the last four seasons (five in college), playoffs and NCAA Tournament included: who leads, average scores and each result. Tap one to open it."],["Live win chance on more games","Live games that ESPN has no win probability for, which is most college games, now show Fullcourt's own live estimate on the card. It starts from the pregame projection and updates with the score and the time left."]]},{id:"2026-11-09b",date:"Nov 9",items:[["Deeper player questions in Ask",`Ask about any split of a player's career and get the per-game averages, a season-by-season table and the full game log: "Brunson stats vs the Spurs", "Luka at home this season", "Tatum in the playoffs", "Curry on the road last season", "Shai in wins", "Jokic in November", "Luka 2023-24" or "Wemby since 2025". Mix them ("Brunson vs the Celtics in the playoffs") or add them to a game search ("Luka 40-point games at home").`]]},{id:"2026-11-09a",date:"Nov 9",items:[["Find any player's games in Ask",`Ask Fullcourt can now search a player's whole career: "Luka 40-point games", "Jokic 30 and 10 this season", "LeBron 30/10/10", "Wemby games with 5+ blocks", "Brunson triple-doubles", "Tatum best scoring games" or "Luka most assists in a game". Add "this season", "in the playoffs" or "vs the Celtics" to narrow it. You get the count, the latest one and a list of the games; tap a game to open it.`]]},{id:"2026-11-08j",date:"Nov 8",items:[["WNBA full game highlights in Replay","WNBA games now get the league's full game highlights from YouTube in Replay, including the playoffs and Finals, and a game's page shows Watch in Replay. This past season's last weeks are in now; next season fills in from May."]]},{id:"2026-11-08i",date:"Nov 8",items:[["Men's college game videos in Replay","Men's college Replay now has the same conference videos as the women's: ACC full game replays and highlights, Big 12 extended highlights and highlights, and Big East highlights, matched to each game. Game pages show Watch in Replay when there's one."]]},{id:"2026-11-08h",date:"Nov 8",items:[["Women's college game videos in Replay","Replay now finds women's college game videos from the ACC, Big 12 and Big East YouTube channels: full game replays and condensed games (ACC), extended highlights (Big 12) and highlights. Each game gets a button for every video there is, and games ESPN has no clip for still show up when a conference does. A game's page shows Watch in Replay when there's a video."],["More NBA full game highlights","NBA full game highlights now come from the NBA's nightly full game highlights list, so far more games have them, plus an Extended button when the NBA posts a longer cut."]]},{id:"2026-11-08g",date:"Nov 8",items:[["Career highs on player pages","Every NBA, WNBA and college player page now has Career highs: their best game for points, rebounds, assists, 3-pointers, steals and blocks, with the opponent, score and date. Tap one to open that game. NBA and WNBA show regular season and playoffs separately, and you also get career counts of 30, 40 and 50-point games, double-doubles and triple-doubles."]]},{id:"2026-11-08f",date:"Nov 8",items:[["Windows app 1.3.2","The mini scoreboard (and the main window) no longer flash plain, unstyled buttons for a moment while opening. The app now has the page's styling in hand before it draws anything."]]},{id:"2026-11-08e",date:"Nov 8",items:[["Win chances on upcoming games","Every upcoming NBA and college game now shows Fullcourt's own chance for each team, from the same ratings as Playoff Odds and Bracketology (injuries and the betting line included). The game's preview shows it next to ESPN's predictor, and NBA team pages show their playoff odds, linking to the full odds page."],["Faster Bet Desk","Rest and back-to-back flags now come from three small requests instead of every team's full schedule (tens of megabytes less on a phone), and the league's player table is kept on your device for a few minutes so Leaders, Compare and the Bet Desk open faster."],["Smoother everywhere","Each section keeps your place: go to Standings and back and Scores is right where you left it (tap the section you're on to jump to the top). Saved to your iPhone's home screen, Scores, Standings and the rest now have pull to refresh. Text fields no longer zoom the page on iPhone, quick taps don't zoom either, and if Fullcourt updates while it's open, it reloads into the new version instead of leaving a button that won't work."],["Fixes and polish","Team tiles show their big background logo as intended, the team stat grid ends cleanly, Bet Desk shows full player names on phones, score cards on laptops fit the top scorer's name, and the header and college tabs fit on the smallest phones. Panels keep the keyboard and screen readers inside them and return you to where you were when they close."],["Windows app 1.3.1","The mini scoreboard now runs the newest Fullcourt from the web too, the app shows a spinner while it starts, and if it opened without a connection it switches to the live site on its own once you're back online. The offline copy of the site keeps more of it, too."]]},{id:"2026-11-08d",date:"Nov 8",items:[["New: Bracketology","College Rankings has a Bracketology tab, for the men's and women's game. Fullcourt plays out the rest of the season 10,000 times, every conference tournament included, picks the field of 68 like the committee (conference champions plus the best at-large resumes) and plays the tournament. You get the projected bracket with the First Four, every team's chance to make the field, its likely seed and its odds of each round, the bubble (last four in, first four out), and each conference's favorites. Updated twice a day."],["Sim the tournament","One tap plays the projected bracket once, from the First Four to the title game, upsets and all. Tap any team for its seed range, odds over time and what its rating is built on."]]},{id:"2026-11-08c",date:"Nov 8",items:[["Smarter playoff odds","Team ratings now blend ESPN's Basketball Power Index with Fullcourt's own scoring margin, adjusted for who each team played and where, with recent games counting more. Injured players are taken out of the games they'll miss (until their expected return), teams get credit for games their regulars sat out, and today's games use the betting line. Standings follow the NBA's real tiebreakers, and the odds now come from 20,000 simulated seasons."],["Tap a team in Odds","Each team has its own page: projected record and win range, where it's likely to finish (seed by seed), its odds over time, how its next game swings them, and a breakdown of why its rating is what it is, with injured players listed. The table also shows each team's seed range at a glance."]]},{id:"2026-11-08b",date:"Nov 8",items:[["New: Playoff odds","Standings has an Odds tab. Fullcourt plays out the rest of the season thousands of times, Play-In and playoffs included, and shows each team's projected record, its chances at the playoffs, the Play-In, the #1 seed, the conference finals, the Finals and the title. It updates every few hours as games finish."],["Sim the season","One tap plays the rest of the season once: final standings, the Play-In, every playoff series and the champion. Tap again for a different outcome."],["Projected draft order","The NBA Mock Draft can now use the projected final standings instead of today's (Today / Projected at the top), with traded picks still applied."],["Data status","Settings shows whether Fullcourt's data, ESPN's feeds and the websites are all working. A check runs every 6 hours and flags anything that breaks or goes stale."]]},{id:"2026-11-08a",date:"Nov 8",items:[["Coaches and front offices","On any NBA or WNBA team page, tap the head coach's name. You get their record this season, with the team and in their career, playoff record and titles, every season they've coached, their awards, the jobs that got them here, and, for NBA teams, who runs the front office, their record in charge, and the team's recent trades."],["Arrange the Scores page","Settings now has a Scores page section: move My bets, Your players, the games, Top scorers, the Conference race, Pick'em and Who's out up or down, and switch off any you don't want (the Conference race can now be hidden too)."],["The Windows app updates itself","From this version on, the app runs the newest Fullcourt straight from the web, so new features and fixes show up on their own without installing anything. Your saved data stays where it is, and if you're offline it opens the copy built into the app."]]},{id:"2026-11-07n",date:"Nov 7",items:[["Photo fix","Legend cards in History now always show the photo the player's profile shows. Some, like Gary Payton's, were falling back to initials."]]},{id:"2026-11-07m",date:"Nov 7",items:[["Nicknames",`Players now show their real nicknames, the ones Basketball-Reference lists (Wemby, The Answer, His Airness...), on player pages, legend cards and History profiles. Search works with them too: type "The Answer" or "Wemby" and the player comes up. Players without a known nickname just don't show one.`]]},{id:"2026-11-07l",date:"Nov 7",items:[["WNBA History","History now covers the WNBA too: games on any date back to 2002, every champion and MVP since 1997, past standings and stat leaders, the all-time career leader boards with a milestone watch, and 74 legends with full profiles, from Cynthia Cooper and Lisa Leslie to Taurasi, Bird and A'ja Wilson. Switch to the WNBA and open History."],["Traded picks in the Mock Draft",`The NBA mock now uses who actually owns each first-round pick, including protections and swaps (the Thunder, Rockets, Hornets and Grizzlies picks, the Jazz-Cavaliers-Timberwolves group and more), with "via" showing whose pick it was. The WNBA mock now follows the league's real 2027 lottery: seven teams, two picks drawn, with Washington holding Chicago's pick and Los Angeles holding Phoenix's.`],["Polish","Cap lines label cleanly on phones, and a check across every section on phone, desktop, light and dark turned up nothing else broken."]]},{id:"2026-11-07k",date:"Nov 7",items:[["New: Mock Draft","A mock draft for the NBA and the WNBA (a Draft tab on wide screens, under More on smaller ones, and in the menu on phones). Fullcourt fills every pick from the standings, taking the best player left and leaning toward what each team needs. Change any pick and the rest re-flow around it, run the lottery as many times as you like, and share your first round as an image. Tap any prospect for their college stats and bio. Prospect rankings come from college stats for now, and switch to ESPN's big board once ESPN publishes it."]]},{id:"2026-11-07j",date:"Nov 7",items:[["Photos for Dave Bing, Fred Brown, Sleepy Floyd, World B. Free and Fat Lever","Five more classic players now have photos in History."],["123 more photos","Dennis Johnson, Lenny Wilkens, Kevin McHale, Walt Frazier, Earl Monroe, Chris Webber, Shawn Kemp and over a hundred more players now have real photos across History, including the Records lists. Nearly everyone on the all-time leader boards has a face now."]]},{id:"2026-11-07i",date:"Nov 7",items:[["55 more classic photos","Magic, Bird, Kareem, Wilt, Russell, Dr. J, Oscar, Jerry West, Hakeem, Barkley, Iverson, Isiah and dozens more legends now have real photos across History, cut out and framed to match the rest of the site."]]},{id:"2026-11-07h",date:"Nov 7",items:[["Michael Jordan's photo","Jordan now has a real photo everywhere in History: his profile, the records, the legends grid and On this day. More classic players' photos are on the way."]]},{id:"2026-11-07g",date:"Nov 7",items:[["History, polished","On this day opens with the date's biggest night as a big spotlight, and arrows step a day back or forward. Seasons shows the champion with its logo and colours, cards for the Finals MVP and the MVP, and arrows to step through seasons. Records puts the top three on a podium, with bars for everyone else. Legend cards show career points, rebounds and assists, and can be sorted by all-time points, titles, MVPs, career scoring or name. Profiles add the teams a player played for and their best season. History also opens on the part you used last."],["Photos for more players","Every Finals MVP now has a full profile and photo, and more players are matched to their ESPN photos (accented names like Joki\u0107 were being missed). ESPN has no photos for many retired greats (Jordan, Bird, Magic and others), so they now get a card in their team's colours with their initials and team logo."],["Clearer cap lines","Cap bars now fill in colour, zone by zone: green under the cap, blue over it, yellow as a taxpayer, orange past the 1st apron and red past the 2nd. The cap, tax and apron lines are drawn in colour too, and a labelled scale sits above the team list."]]},{id:"2026-11-07f",date:"Nov 7",items:[["New: History","A whole new section for the NBA's past (a History tab on wide screens, under More on smaller ones, and in the menu on phones). On this day: every game played on today's date back to 2001, the biggest scoring nights, the closest finishes and legends born today, and you can pick any date. Seasons: every champion, Finals MVP and MVP since 1950, plus final standings and stat leaders from 2001-02 on. Records: the all-time career leader boards and a milestone watch for active players closing in on someone. Legends: the all-time greats with photos, and a search for any player past or present."],["Player profiles for anyone","Tap any name in History for a full profile: photo, bio, accolades, career averages, where they rank all-time, points per game season by season, their full season-by-season stats, and a link to watch their career highlights."]]},{id:"2026-11-07e",date:"Nov 7",items:[["Full game highlights in Replay","NBA games in Replay get a Full game button for the NBA's full-length highlights (usually around 10 minutes), playing right in the card. All Replay videos now start muted; tap the speaker for sound."]]},{id:"2026-11-07d",date:"Nov 7",items:[["More room on big screens","On wide screens (1640 px and up) the whole site is a bit wider, and Compare is back as its own tab in the header. Laptops, tablets and phones look the same as before."]]},{id:"2026-11-07c",date:"Nov 7",items:[["Leaders stay current","League leaders now refresh on their own while the page is open: every minute while games are live, every 10 minutes otherwise, and right after any game ends (season stats count finished games). The board updates in place without jumping, and a line under the title shows when it last updated. The same goes for the advanced boards and award races."]]},{id:"2026-11-07b",date:"Nov 7",items:[["Capsheet: every NBA contract","A new Cap tab has every team's cap sheet: each player's salary for the next six seasons, player and team options, non-guaranteed years, dead money from waived players and two-way deals, with the team's payroll against the cap, tax line and both aprons. The Players tab is searchable and sortable by team, salary, money left and contract end (try Expires after 2026-27 for next summer's free agents). Tap anyone for their full contract. NBA player pages now have a Contract card too. Contracts refresh every Monday."],["Deadline: the trade machine","Inside Cap, Trade machine lets you pick 2 to 4 teams, move players and draft picks, and see right away whether the deal works under 2026-27 rules: salary matching, the first and second aprons, cap room, roster limits, trade kickers and recently signed free agents, with a plain-English reason when it doesn't. Each team shows its payroll before and after. Save trades on your device or share a trade card image."],["Chalk: a live 2D court","Every game has a new Court tab (and a Court button on live and finished games on Scores): a top-down court where shots land as they happen, made or missed in team colors, building a running shot chart next to the scorebug and play log. Finished games replay at 1\xD7 to 60\xD7 with play, pause, a scrubber and quarter jumps; live games follow along. Tap any play in the log to jump there."]]},{id:"2026-11-07a",date:"Nov 7",items:[["Replay: every game's highlights","A new Replay tab is a clean feed of each finished game's highlights, newest first, with the final score on every card. Filter by team or jump to a date, scroll for older days, and open Top plays for the game's individual clips. Nothing plays until you tap, and a video pauses when you scroll past it. Finished games on Scores now show a Highlights marker, and the game sheet has a Highlights in Replay button. Works for the WNBA and college too."],["Compare moved to More","To make room for Replay, Compare is now in the More menu at the end of the header (and still in the phone menu)."]]},{id:"2026-11-06e",date:"Nov 6",items:[["Move your data anywhere","Settings \u2192 Your data can now export everything you've saved (tracked bets, stars, favorites, your players, Pick'em and settings) as a file or copied text, and import it in another browser, on another device or in the Windows app."],["Mini scoreboard (Windows app)","A small always-on-top window with today's games and your tracked bets, live. Open it from the new header button, Settings or the tray icon. Pin or unpin it on top, and jump back to the full window any time."],["Runs in the tray (Windows app)","Closing the Windows app now keeps Fullcourt in the tray by the clock, so bet alerts keep coming. Click the icon to bring it back; right-click for Mini scoreboard, Bet desk or Quit. Turn it off in Settings if you'd rather it quit."]]},{id:"2026-11-06d",date:"Nov 6",items:[["Check for updates (Windows app)","In the Windows app, Settings has a Windows app section with your version and a Check for updates button. If a new version is out, the same row becomes Update now: it downloads, installs and reopens Fullcourt for you. Release notes for every version are one tap away."]]},{id:"2026-11-06c",date:"Nov 6",items:[["Switch markets inside a prop","Prop detail has a market picker at the top of Game by game. Jump from P+R to points, rebounds, 3PA or any other stat without leaving the view: the line (tonight's real one when there is one), hit rates, chart and minutes projection all switch, and your Over/Under, range, home/away, opponent and teammate filters stay."]]},{id:"2026-11-06b",date:"Nov 6",items:[["Real lines and fair prices for FGA, 3PA and 2PT","Shot-attempt and 2-pointer props now use the market's consensus line (marked MKT) from the pick'em apps that set them, instead of Fullcourt's estimate. No sportsbook on our feed prices them, so the Over/Under column shows a fair price instead: how often he's cleared that line in his last 20 games, turned into odds. Add one to a slip and it uses that fair price; you can still type your own."]]},{id:"2026-11-06a",date:"Nov 6",items:[["Fullcourt for Windows","Fullcourt is now also a Windows app: the same site in its own window, with live scores, odds and props, and bet alerts as Windows notifications. Outside links open in your normal browser. Download Fullcourt-Setup.exe from the link below and run it (if Windows says it protected your PC, click More info, then Run anyway). The app lets you know when a new version is out. Your bets, stars and favorites live separately in the app and the browser.",["Get it for Windows","https://github.com/larosa023/fullcourt/releases/latest"]]]},{id:"2026-11-04b",date:"Nov 4",items:[["With / without on player pages","Every NBA and WNBA player page has a With / without card: his points, rebounds, assists and minutes in games each of his main teammates missed, and how that compares with games they played together. Biggest swings first; tap a teammate to open his page."],["Minutes projection on props","Prop detail now projects his minutes tonight from his last 5, last 10 and season, adjusted for a back-to-back, a lopsided spread and any teammates ruled out (using how his minutes changed when they sat before). It shows the likely range, every adjustment, and the stat he'd get at his recent per-minute rate, which also appears under the line at the top."]]},{id:"2026-11-04a",date:"Nov 4",items:[["Teammate in / out on props","In a prop's detail view, pick any teammate under Game by game to see only the games he missed, then tap his chip to flip to games he played. The chart and the L5, L10, L15 and season hit rates all update. Stack more than one teammate, and anyone ruled out tonight shows up as a one-tap suggestion."],["All-Star games left out","All-Star games no longer show up in player game logs, prop charts or season highs."]]},{id:"2026-11-03f",date:"Nov 3",items:[["Bet milestone alerts","Tracked bets now give you a heads-up while games are live: when a player is one basket (or one rebound, steal and so on) away from hitting an over, when an over still needs more in the last five minutes, and when an under is about to be blown. Each alert fires once per leg. With notifications on and the site in the background, they come as notifications."],["Tap a leg for the box score","Tap any player leg on a tracked bet to open that game straight to his team's box score, with his row highlighted."]]},{id:"2026-11-03e",date:"Nov 3",items:[["Share a stat line","Every player in a box score (and every game in a player's season game log) has a small share icon. It makes a clean image of that game: photo over the team colours, the matchup and final score, points, rebounds and assists up big, then steals, blocks, turnovers, minutes, shooting and +/-, with a badge for a double-double, triple-double or season high. On a computer it's copied, ready to paste; on a phone it opens the share sheet."],["Sharper share images","All share images (bets, comparisons, games) now use the condensed headline font like the rest of the site."]]},{id:"2026-11-03d",date:"Nov 3",items:[["College player splits","College player pages have new Splits: pick any season to see home and away, wins and losses, conference vs non-conference games, games against AP Top 25 teams (ranked on the day they played), and month by month, with an Advanced view. Below it, career highs (points, rebounds, assists, threes, steals, blocks) from every college season, each a tap away from the box score."]]},{id:"2026-11-03c",date:"Nov 3",items:[["NBA Cup","Standings has an NBA Cup tab: all six groups with the official tiebreakers (head-to-head, point differential with overtime games counting as zero, points scored), wild cards marked, and the knockout bracket, projected during group play and filled in with real games in December. Cup games on the Scores page are tagged with their group."],["College bracket","Rankings has a Bracket tab for men's and women's: the NCAA Tournament by region plus the Final Four, and every conference tournament round by round, with live scores. Last season's brackets are there until this season's start."],["Top 25 clashes and upsets","College scores have a Top 25 clashes filter for ranked-vs-ranked games, and Upset tags (on cards, the ticker and alerts) when a ranked team loses to an unranked one, or to a much lower seed in March."]]},{id:"2026-11-03b",date:"Nov 3",items:[["Faster loading","Fonts now come from Fullcourt itself instead of Google, today's scores and standings start downloading the moment the page opens, and team logos are fetched once and reused everywhere (about half as many image downloads on a full night)."],["College polish",`Ask understands "Top 25" and polls, uses college-style answers ("The Gamecocks play next\u2026", "leads Division I"), and has college example questions. College days only load the Top 25 games in the Pick'em and injury panels, and saved scores work offline for college too.`],["Header fit","The top bar now lines up with the page edges at every screen size, with or without a favorite team chip."]]},{id:"2026-11-03a",date:"Nov 3",items:[["College basketball","Tap NCAA in the league switch (or the menu on your phone) for women's and men's college hoops, with a Women | Men toggle beside it. Scores open on games with a ranked team, with every Division I game and each conference a pick away. Rankings has the AP and Coaches polls plus all 32 conference standings, Teams lists every school by conference, and games, box scores, play-by-play, win probability and team pages all work like they do for the pros."]]},{id:"2026-11-01d",date:"Nov 1",items:[["More sportsbooks","The Bet desk now pulls lines from FanDuel, ESPN BET and other books a few times a day. A new Best column shows the friendliest line and price across books, and when DraftKings hasn't posted a prop yet you get the real FanDuel (or other book) line instead of an estimate. The prop breakdown has a By book card to compare every book at a glance."]]},{id:"2026-11-01c",date:"Nov 1",items:[["Matchup card","Every prop breakdown now has a Matchup card: with/without numbers when a key teammate is out (his per-36 with that player on vs off the floor), game pace, rest, blowout risk, and for scoring props his shot zones against what tonight's defense allows there. Free data from PBPStats and ESPN."],["Minutes overlay","Tap MIN on the game-by-game chart to lay his minutes over every bar."],["New Bet desk flags","Rows now flag back-to-backs, 3 games in 4 nights, fast or slow matchups, and blowout risk for starters."],["First basket","Each game on the Game lines tab has a First basket section: how often each team gets the first possession and scores first, and who usually makes their first basket."],["Export to your book","The parlay slip has an Export button for DraftKings, FanDuel, Fanatics, Hard Rock, theScore Bet, bet365, PrizePicks and Sleeper. It copies your picks in that app's wording and opens it."]]},{id:"2026-11-01b",date:"Nov 1",items:[["New prop charts","The prop breakdown has a new game-by-game chart: green and red bars against your line, a dotted bar for games he sat, and L5 / L10 / L15 / Season / vs-opponent hit rates you can tap to change the range. Filter by home/away or opponent."],["Rebound and assist detail","Rebound bars now split offensive and defensive boards, with his share of available rebounds, and assist props show assist points, 3-point assists and at-rim assists, from PBPStats play-by-play."]]},{id:"2026-11-01a",date:"Nov 1",items:[["Share your bets","A share button on every bet card and on the parlay slip makes a clean image of the bet. On a phone it opens the share sheet; on a computer it copies the image so you can paste it straight into a chat."],["Live props","Once a game tips, every prop in the Bet desk shows his number so far and where he's pacing, green when it's on track and a check once it hits."],["Under the radar","A new Bet desk filter that shows only role players (under 15 a game) whose minutes have climbed lately, where lines tend to lag."]]},{id:"2026-10-31h",date:"Oct 31",items:[["Bet desk upgrades","Star a prop to pin it to the top and get an alert if its line moves a point or the book posts it. New DvP column (how players at his position do against tonight's defense), minutes-up/down and teammate-out flags, and your market and sort are remembered."],["Alt lines and compare","The prop breakdown now shows the DraftKings alt-line ladder with each rung's implied odds against his real hit rate, and a Compare picker to put two players' last 10 games side by side."],["My bets and Record","Two new Bet desk tabs: My bets (record, profit, ROI, by week, leg hit rate by market, best win, closest call) and Record, which grades Fullcourt's top-Score props and game-line leans after the games."],["Live parlays","Live parlay cards now say what they still need, and you get a heads-up the moment a leg hits or misses."],["Win probability","Live score cards show a win-probability bar."]]},{id:"2026-10-31g",date:"Oct 31",items:[["Bet desk","A new Bets tab: today's DraftKings player props for every market with each player's hit rate on that exact line (last 5, last 10, season, vs tonight's opponent), averages, opponent defense and line moves, plus a Game lines view with projections. Tap a row for the full breakdown or + to track it."],["Themes","The palette button at the top now opens a theme menu: Midnight, Pure black, Hardwood, Forest, Paper, Clean white, Ice and more."]]},{id:"2026-10-31f",date:"Oct 31",items:[["Prop ideas in Ask",`Ask "best props tonight", "Knicks game picks" or "Wembanyama props" for players who keep clearing their marks, matchup and injury notes, and how each game line compares with the teams' scoring. Tap + to track one.`],["Game log totals","The season game log now has a Totals row, and shooting percentages in the averages."]]},{id:"2026-10-31e",date:"Oct 31",items:[["Award races","MVP, Rookie, Defensive Player and Sixth Man races now blend sportsbook odds, the ESPN panel and staff picks from The Ringer, SI and Bleacher Report with Fullcourt's stats model, with stats on every row and sources listed."],["Track your bets","Type a bet or paste a slip screenshot into Ask to follow it live under My bets on Scores."]]},{id:"2026-10-31d",date:"Oct 31",items:[["Advanced stats","An Advanced switch on box scores (TS%, eFG%, usage, game score), team stats (ratings, pace, four factors), player splits, game logs and career stats (efficiency, shot profile, per 36), team rankings and Leaders. It remembers your choice everywhere."],["Team leaders","Team pages show the team's top 5 in any stat. Tap Points, Rebounds, Assists, Steals, Blocks, 3-pointers, FG% or Minutes to switch."],["Recent form","Team pages chart the last 10 games. Tap Margin, Points scored or Points allowed; tap a bar to open that game."],["Season game log","Player pages have an expandable log of every game this season, filterable by wins, losses, home, away, 20+ point games and double-doubles."],["Roster moves","A new Moves tab on Teams lists signings, trades and waivers league-wide, filterable by type and team. Team pages show their own recent moves."],["Settings","New Settings panel (sliders icon in the header, or the phone menu): switch off odds, Pick'em, Who's out, Your players, Top scorers or the ticker, pick a theme, and reset your data."],["This week","Every game for the next 7 days on one page, with national TV and lines. Filter to just your team."],["Where to watch","Upcoming and live games list their channels, with links to the official ESPN, Prime Video, Peacock and League Pass pages."],["Cleanup","Removed leftover code from earlier features and tidied styles."],["Career stats","Player pages have a Career stats section: tap to expand season-by-season numbers, with playoffs and a show-all for long careers."],["Game header fits","Scores and team names no longer overlap at the top of a game."]]},{id:"2026-10-30c",date:"Oct 30",items:[["Mini scoreboard removed","The pop-out mini scoreboard has been taken out."],["Faster loading","The site now loads about 40% less up front. Extras like Ask, Compare, rankings and sharing load the first time you open them, and updates only re-download what changed."],["Big nights moved into the game","40-point games, triple-doubles and comebacks now show inside the game (under the recap) instead of as a tag on the score cards."]]},{id:"2026-10-29d",date:"Oct 29",items:[["Team-colored leader bars","Bars on the Leaders page (and the MVP and Rookie races) use each player's team color."],["Injured section","Injured players sit in their own section at the bottom of the box score instead of with the bench."],["Mini scoreboard","Pop today's scores into a small window. In Chrome and Edge it stays on top of your other apps."],["Your players","Star any player to follow their live stat line in a strip at the top of Scores."],["Who's out","Injury report for every game on the day, in one panel on the Scores page."],["Line movement","Arrows on game cards show how the spread and total moved since opening. Previews get a full line movement card."],["Pick'em","Pick the winners of each game. Picks lock at tip-off and your record and streak are tracked."],["Game recaps","Every finished game opens with a short summary written from the box score."],["Team rankings","Teams page has a Rankings tab: every team ranked in 14 stats, sortable by column."],["Copy as image","On a computer the share button now copies the picture, ready to paste."],["What's new","This list."]]},{id:"2026-10-29a",date:"Oct 29 (overnight)",items:[["Win probability","Biggest swings are marked, and you can hover the chart to read any moment."],["Play-by-play filters","Scoring plays only, either team, any quarter."],["Game previews","Win chance, last 5 games, season series and the stats where teams differ most."],["Highlights","ESPN clips inside finished games. They start muted."],["Officials","The referee crew for every game."],["Big-night badges","40-point games, triple-doubles and big comebacks are flagged on the score cards."],["Team alerts","Notifications for your team at tip-off, overtime, close finishes and the final."],["Player trends","Last 10 games chart plus home/away and win/loss splits."],["Team calendar","Month view with back-to-backs and road trips marked."],["MVP and Rookie races","Fullcourt's own estimate, under Leaders."],["Home screen app","New icon and loading screen, and saved scores when you have no signal."],["Share images","Share a final score or a player card as a picture."]]},{id:"2026-10-28",date:"Oct 28",items:[["WNBA mode","Switch between NBA and WNBA from the header or the menu (shortcut L). Each league is its own mode."],["Timeouts and bonus","Live games show timeouts left, when a team is in the bonus, and when a timeout is on."],["Jersey numbers","Shown next to every player in the box score."],["Who's on the court","Live box scores list the five players on the floor first."],["Injuries","Injury report on team pages, and injured players in red at the bottom of box scores."]]},{id:"2026-10-27",date:"Oct 27",items:[["Tan light mode","Easier on the eyes than bright white."],["Back button","Mouse, keyboard and swipe Back close the open panel."],["Ask Fullcourt","Type stats questions in plain English."],["Desktop upgrades","Score ticker, multi-view, shot charts, game flow, search, keyboard shortcuts, favorite team, Compare and the playoff picture."],["Phone menu","A side menu replaces the bottom tab bar."],["Full-screen games","Expand any game to the whole screen."],["Shooting splits","Made/attempted and percentages for FG, 3PT and FT in box scores."],["Odds","Moneyline, spread and total on every game."],["Eastern time","Times in ET, and the day rolls over at 4 AM so late games stay on last night's slate."],["Fullcourt launched","Live scores, standings, teams, rosters, stats and light/dark mode."]]}];function p(){const n=c("What's new");n.body.innerHTML=`<div class="news">${t.map((s,o)=>`
    <section class="news-day enter" style="--i:${o}">
      <div class="news-date"><span>${e(s.date)}</span>${o===0?"<em>Latest</em>":""}</div>
      <ul>${s.items.map(([r,i,a])=>`<li><b>${e(r)}</b><span>${e(i)}${a?` <a href="${e(a[1])}" target="_blank" rel="noopener">${e(a[0])} \u2192</a>`:""}</span></li>`).join("")}</ul>
    </section>`).join("")}</div>`,d(h,t[0].id),l()}export{t as UPDATES,p as openNews};
